    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">ERRIRQCR&lt;m&gt;, n = 0 - 15</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Generic Error Interrupt Configuration Register &lt;m&gt;</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>The ERRIRQCR&lt;m&gt; registers are reserved for <span class="arm-defined-word">IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</span> interrupt configuration registers.</p>

      
        <p>The architecture provides a recommended layout for the ERRIRQCR&lt;m&gt; registers. These registers are named:</p>

      
        <ul>
<li><a href="ext-errfhicr0.html">ERRFHICR0</a>, <a href="ext-errfhicr1.html">ERRFHICR1</a>, and <a href="ext-errfhicr2.html">ERRFHICR2</a> for the fault handling interrupt controls.
</li><li><a href="ext-errericr0.html">ERRERICR0</a>, <a href="ext-errericr1.html">ERRERICR1</a>, and <a href="ext-errericr2.html">ERRERICR2</a> for the error recovery interrupt controls.
</li><li><a href="ext-errcricr0.html">ERRCRICR0</a>, <a href="ext-errcricr1.html">ERRCRICR1</a>, and <a href="ext-errcricr2.html">ERRCRICR2</a> for the critical error interrupt controls.
</li><li><a href="ext-errirqsr.html">ERRIRQSR</a> for the status register.
</li></ul>

      
        <p>This section describes the generic, <span class="arm-defined-word">IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</span>, format.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>This register is present only when FEAT_RASSA_IRQCR is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to ERRIRQCR&lt;m&gt; are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
        <p>ERRIRQCR&lt;m&gt; is implemented only as part of a memory-mapped group of error records.</p>
      <h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>ERRIRQCR&lt;m&gt; is a 64-bit register.</p>
